          "content": "A) Stay in the city. \n\nLeaving the city does nothing to alleviate or end the child's suffering; it merely adds to the total amount of misery in the world by stripping away your own well-being and causing grief to the family and friends you leave behind. Walking away is a purely symbolic gesture that produces a worse overall outcome. Because staying preserves the immense, collective happiness of thousands of thriving lives\u2014including your own\u2014it results in far greater overall well-being and prevents an unnecessary increase in net suffering.",
